IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`

-- P1-art5: Article 5(1) of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744):
-- the prohibited AI practices, points (a) to (h), the points the Omnibus inserted ((ba), (bb)) and the paragraphs it inserted (1a, 1b).
-- Paragraphs 2 to 8 are in P1-art5-rbi.
-- THE OMNIBUS added points (ba) and (bb), and paragraphs 1a and 1b (the lines below the marker "M1 INSERTED" in the consolidated text). Those four exist as amended
-- only and apply from 2 December 2026 (provision group `Article 5 additions`); points (a) to (h) are the same in both texts and apply from 2 February 2025
-- (provision group `Chapter II`). Article 111(2) cannot save either group, so the gate takes the constants for the route and the placement date.
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER. Each point is a function that answers MAYBE BOOLEAN:
--   JUST TRUE   the facts are the practice the point prohibits;
--   JUST FALSE  the text says in its own words that the case is not prohibited: the carve-out of the point or of paragraph 1a or 1b
--               ("shall not apply", "except where", "does not cover", "unless", "only prohibited where", "shall not constitute");
--   NOTHING     the practice is not covered: the Article does not yet apply on the date asked, or an element of the practice is missing
--               (an unmet element of a prohibition is not the text's own "no"; fork F-5-1-element, split site (i)).
-- The act is a plain input: the placing on the market, the putting into service or the use. Where the point says "putting into service for this specific purpose",
-- the specific purpose is a condition of the putting into service only (fork F-5-1-specific-purpose).
-- Terms the Regulation defines in Article 3 (a biometric categorisation system, a 'real-time' remote biometric identification system, publicly accessible space, law enforcement, biometric data) are
-- BOOLEAN inputs of these functions, so that each function is testable one fact at a time. The seat layer (P1-seat-*.l4) works each term out from the facts that the keel's Article 3 function takes,
-- by calling that function, and passes it on (fork F-5-3-defined-terms; seam S16).

§ `Article 5: the gates (Article 113 and the provision groups)`

-- Article 5 as it was enacted applies from 2 February 2025 (Article 113 third paragraph, point (a)): provision group `Chapter II`.
-- src:1660 | (a) Chapters I and II shall apply from 2 February 2025, with the exception of Article 5(1), first subparagraph, points (ba) and (bb), and Article 5(1a) and (1b) which shall apply from 2 December 2026;
@ref Art 113 third paragraph point (a), for Article 5 (src:1660)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 5 the Chapter II provisions apply on the date asked` MEANS
    `Art 113 the provision group applies` `Chapter II` `the date asked` `the route to pass when no AI system is in question` `the date to pass when no AI system is in question` FALSE

-- The four insertions (ba), (bb), 1a, 1b apply from 2 December 2026 (provision group `Article 5 additions`).
-- src:1660 | (a) Chapters I and II shall apply from 2 February 2025, with the exception of Article 5(1), first subparagraph, points (ba) and (bb), and Article 5(1a) and (1b) which shall apply from 2 December 2026;
@ref Art 113 third paragraph point (a), the insertions of Article 5 (src:1660)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 5 the Article 5 additions apply on the date asked` MEANS
    `Art 113 the provision group applies` `Article 5 additions` `the date asked` `the route to pass when no AI system is in question` `the date to pass when no AI system is in question` FALSE

§ `Article 5(1): the act, and what "for this specific purpose" attaches to`

-- "the placing on the market, the putting into service or the use": the three acts of the first subparagraph.
DECLARE `Art 5(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 5(1) act placing on the market`
    `Art 5(1) act putting into service`
    `Art 5(1) act use`

-- Points (d) to (g) say "the putting into service for this specific purpose": the qualifier belongs to the putting into service only.
-- The placing on the market and the use need no specific purpose (fork F-5-1-specific-purpose).
GIVEN `the act` IS AN `Art 5(1) act`
      `the putting into service is for this specific purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 5(1) the act is within the practice` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the act`
    WHEN `Art 5(1) act putting into service` THEN `the putting into service is for this specific purpose`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§ `Article 5(1)(a): subliminal, manipulative and deceptive techniques`

-- fork F-5-1-a-purposefully: "purposefully manipulative or deceptive techniques" can mean (A) purposefully manipulative, or purposefully deceptive, or (B) purposefully manipulative, or deceptive without purpose.
-- The input is the text's own phrase, so the caller states whether the technique is within it; reading A (the narrower) is the one the input's name carries.
-- src:176 | (a) the placing on the market, the putting into service or the use of an AI system that deploys subliminal techniques beyond a person’s consciousness or purposefully manipulative or deceptive techniques, with the objective, or the effect of materially distorting the behaviour of a person or a group of persons by appreciably impairing their ability to make an informed decision, thereby causing them to take a decision that they would not have otherwise taken in a manner that causes or is reasonably likely to cause that person, another person or group of persons significant harm;
@ref Art 5(1) first subparagraph point (a) (src:176)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system deploys subliminal techniques beyond a person's consciousness` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system deploys purposefully manipulative or deceptive techniques` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technique has the objective, or the effect, of materially distorting the behaviour of a person or a group of persons by appreciably impairing their ability to make an informed decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person or group of persons is thereby caused to take a decision that they would not have otherwise taken` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is taken in a manner that causes or is reasonably likely to cause that person, another person or group of persons significant harm` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 5(1)(a) the AI practice is prohibited` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 5 the Chapter II provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 5 applies from 2 February 2025 (Article 113 third paragraph, point (a))
        IF NOT (    (   `the AI system deploys subliminal techniques beyond a person's consciousness`
                     OR `the AI system deploys purposefully manipulative or deceptive techniques`)
                AND `the technique has the objective, or the effect, of materially distorting the behaviour of a person or a group of persons by appreciably impairing their ability to make an informed decision`
                AND `the person or group of persons is thereby caused to take a decision that they would not have otherwise taken`
                AND `the decision is taken in a manner that causes or is reasonably likely to cause that person, another person or group of persons significant harm`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): an element of the prohibited practice is missing; the text prohibits the practice described and says nothing of one that lacks an element
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Article 5(1)(b): exploiting vulnerabilities`

-- src:177 | (b) the placing on the market, the putting into service or the use of an AI system that exploits any of the vulnerabilities of a natural person or a specific group of persons due to their age, disability or a specific social or economic situation, with the objective, or the effect, of materially distorting the behaviour of that person or a person belonging to that group in a manner that causes or is reasonably likely to cause that person or another person significant harm;
@ref Art 5(1) first subparagraph point (b) (src:177)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system exploits any of the vulnerabilities of a natural person or a specific group of persons due to their age, disability or a specific social or economic situation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system has the objective, or the effect, of materially distorting the behaviour of that person or a person belonging to that group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the distortion is in a manner that causes or is reasonably likely to cause that person or another person significant harm` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 5(1)(b) the AI practice is prohibited` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 5 the Chapter II provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 5 applies from 2 February 2025 (Article 113 third paragraph, point (a))
        IF NOT (    `the AI system exploits any of the vulnerabilities of a natural person or a specific group of persons due to their age, disability or a specific social or economic situation`
                AND `the AI system has the objective, or the effect, of materially distorting the behaviour of that person or a person belonging to that group`
                AND `the distortion is in a manner that causes or is reasonably likely to cause that person or another person significant harm`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): an element of the prohibited practice is missing
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Article 5(1)(ba) and (bb), paragraphs 1a and 1b (inserted by the Omnibus; apply from 2 December 2026)`

-- Paragraph 1a: "For the purposes of paragraph 1, first subparagraph, points (ba) and (bb)" the placing on the market or putting into service is "only prohibited where"
-- (i) the generation or manipulation is the intended purpose, or (ii) it is a reasonably foreseeable and reproducible outcome AND the system lacks adequate safeguards;
-- the use is "only prohibited where the deployer uses the system for the purpose". A list closed with "only": outside it the text says no.
-- src:195 | 1a. For the purposes of paragraph 1, first subparagraph, points (ba) and (bb):
-- src:196 | (a) the placing on the market or putting into service of an AI system that generates or manipulates the material or performance referred to in paragraph 1, first subparagraph, point (ba) or (bb) is only prohibited where:
-- src:197 | (i) that generation or manipulation is the intended purpose of the AI system; or
-- src:198 | (ii) the system’s design, training, architecture, capabilities or user-facing functionalities make that generation or manipulation a reasonably foreseeable and reproducible outcome, without requiring significant technical modification, and the system does not have reasonable and adequate technical safety measures and other safeguards to reliably prevent that generation or manipulation, taking into account reasonably foreseeable misuse, and to correct observed or reported misuse;
-- src:199 | (b) the use of an AI system that generates or manipulates the material or performance referred to in paragraph 1, first subparagraph, points (ba) and (bb) is only prohibited where the deployer uses the system for the purpose of generating or manipulating such material or performance.
@ref Art 5(1a) for the purposes of points (ba) and (bb) (src:195-199)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the act` IS AN `Art 5(1) act`
      `that generation or manipulation is the intended purpose of the AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the system's design, training, architecture, capabilities or user-facing functionalities make that generation or manipulation a reasonably foreseeable and reproducible outcome, without requiring significant technical modification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the system has reasonable and adequate technical safety measures and other safeguards to reliably prevent that generation or manipulation, taking into account reasonably foreseeable misuse, and to correct observed or reported misuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deployer uses the system for the purpose of generating or manipulating such material or performance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 5(1a) the act is within the limits that paragraph 1a sets for points (ba) and (bb)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 5 the Article 5 additions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph 1a applies from 2 December 2026 (Article 113 third paragraph, point (a), as the Omnibus amends it)
        IF `the act` EQUALS `Art 5(1) act use`
        THEN JUST `the deployer uses the system for the purpose of generating or manipulating such material or performance`
             -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the use of an AI system that generates or manipulates the material or performance ... is only prohibited where the deployer uses the system for the purpose of generating or manipulating such material or performance"
        OTHERWISE
            JUST (   `that generation or manipulation is the intended purpose of the AI system`
                  OR (    `the system's design, training, architecture, capabilities or user-facing functionalities make that generation or manipulation a reasonably foreseeable and reproducible outcome, without requiring significant technical modification`
                      AND (NOT `the system has reasonable and adequate technical safety measures and other safeguards to reliably prevent that generation or manipulation, taking into account reasonably foreseeable misuse, and to correct observed or reported misuse`)))
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the placing on the market or putting into service of an AI system that generates or manipulates the material or performance ... is only prohibited where"

-- fork F-5-1b-reach: paragraph 1b says a system that manipulates material without increasing the exposure of intimate parts or altering the nature of sexually explicit activities "shall not constitute manipulation".
-- Reading taken: it excuses a system that only manipulates; a system that also generates such material is still within point (ba) (the other reading: 1b excuses the whole system).
-- src:179 | (ba) the placing on the market, the putting into service or the use of an AI system that generates or manipulates realistic images, videos, audio or similar material of an identifiable natural person’s intimate parts, or of an identifiable natural person engaged in sexually explicit activities, without that person’s freely-given, specific, informed, unambiguous and explicit consent for that generation or manipulation;
@ref Art 5(1) first subparagraph point (ba) (src:179)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the act` IS AN `Art 5(1) act`
      `the AI system generates realistic images, videos, audio or similar material` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system manipulates realistic images, videos, audio or similar material` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the material is of an identifiable natural person's intimate parts, or of an identifiable natural person engaged in sexually explicit activities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has given freely-given, specific, informed, unambiguous and explicit consent for that generation or manipulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the manipulation does not increase the exposure of any depicted intimate parts or alter the nature of any depicted sexually explicit activities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that generation or manipulation is the intended purpose of the AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the system's design, training, architecture, capabilities or user-facing functionalities make that generation or manipulation a reasonably foreseeable and reproducible outcome, without requiring significant technical modification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the system has reasonable and adequate technical safety measures and other safeguards to reliably prevent that generation or manipulation, taking into account reasonably foreseeable misuse, and to correct observed or reported misuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deployer uses the system for the purpose of generating or manipulating such material or performance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 5(1)(ba) the AI practice is prohibited` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 5 the Article 5 additions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): point (ba) applies from 2 December 2026 (Article 113 third paragraph, point (a), as the Omnibus amends it)
        IF NOT (    (`the AI system generates realistic images, videos, audio or similar material` OR `the AI system manipulates realistic images, videos, audio or similar material`)
                AND `the material is of an identifiable natural person's intimate parts, or of an identifiable natural person engaged in sexually explicit activities`
                AND (NOT `the person has given freely-given, specific, informed, unambiguous and explicit consent for that generation or manipulation`))
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): an element is missing (the material, or the absence of the person's consent); the text prohibits the practice described
        IF     (NOT `the AI system generates realistic images, videos, audio or similar material`)
           AND `the manipulation does not increase the exposure of any depicted intimate parts or alter the nature of any depicted sexually explicit activities`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an AI system that manipulates material in a way that does not increase the exposure of any depicted intimate parts or alter the nature of any depicted sexually explicit activities shall not constitute manipulation" (paragraph 1b)
        IF `Art 5(1a) the act is within the limits that paragraph 1a sets for points (ba) and (bb)` `the date asked` `the act` `that generation or manipulation is the intended purpose of the AI system` `the system's design, training, architecture, capabilities or user-facing functionalities make that generation or manipulation a reasonably foreseeable and reproducible outcome, without requiring significant technical modification` `the system has reasonable and adequate technical safety measures and other safeguards to reliably prevent that generation or manipulation, taking into account reasonably foreseeable misuse, and to correct observed or reported misuse` `the deployer uses the system for the purpose of generating or manipulating such material or performance` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is only prohibited where" (paragraph 1a)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:180 | (bb) the placing on the market, the putting into service or the use of an AI system that generates or manipulates material or performance within the meaning of Article 2, points (c) and (e), of Directive 2011/93/EU, except where a ‘without right’ defence applies under national law;
@ref Art 5(1) first subparagraph point (bb) (src:180)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the act` IS AN `Art 5(1) act`
      `the AI system generates or manipulates material or performance within the meaning of Article 2, points (c) and (e), of Directive 2011/93/EU` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a 'without right' defence applies under national law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that generation or manipulation is the intended purpose of the AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the system's design, training, architecture, capabilities or user-facing functionalities make that generation or manipulation a reasonably foreseeable and reproducible outcome, without requiring significant technical modification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the system has reasonable and adequate technical safety measures and other safeguards to reliably prevent that generation or manipulation, taking into account reasonably foreseeable misuse, and to correct observed or reported misuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deployer uses the system for the purpose of generating or manipulating such material or performance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 5(1)(bb) the AI practice is prohibited` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 5 the Article 5 additions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): point (bb) applies from 2 December 2026 (Article 113 third paragraph, point (a), as the Omnibus amends it)
        IF NOT `the AI system generates or manipulates material or performance within the meaning of Article 2, points (c) and (e), of Directive 2011/93/EU`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term, fork F-5-1-bb-directive): "material or performance within the meaning of Article 2, points (c) and (e), of Directive 2011/93/EU" is the Directive's definition, which is not among the sources; the caller states whether the material is within it
        IF `a 'without right' defence applies under national law`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except where a 'without right' defence applies under national law"
        IF `Art 5(1a) the act is within the limits that paragraph 1a sets for points (ba) and (bb)` `the date asked` `the act` `that generation or manipulation is the intended purpose of the AI system` `the system's design, training, architecture, capabilities or user-facing functionalities make that generation or manipulation a reasonably foreseeable and reproducible outcome, without requiring significant technical modification` `the system has reasonable and adequate technical safety measures and other safeguards to reliably prevent that generation or manipulation, taking into account reasonably foreseeable misuse, and to correct observed or reported misuse` `the deployer uses the system for the purpose of generating or manipulating such material or performance` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is only prohibited where" (paragraph 1a)
