§ `Article 5(1)(c): social scoring`

-- src:182 | (c) the placing on the market, the putting into service or the use of AI systems for the evaluation or classification of natural persons or groups of persons over a certain period of time based on their social behaviour or known, inferred or predicted personal or personality characteristics, with the social score leading to either or both of the following:
-- src:183 | (i) detrimental or unfavourable treatment of certain natural persons or groups of persons in social contexts that are unrelated to the contexts in which the data was originally generated or collected;
-- src:184 | (ii) detrimental or unfavourable treatment of certain natural persons or groups of persons that is unjustified or disproportionate to their social behaviour or its gravity;
@ref Art 5(1) first subparagraph point (c) (src:182-184)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system is for the evaluation or classification of natural persons or groups of persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evaluation or classification is over a certain period of time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evaluation or classification is based on their social behaviour or known, inferred or predicted personal or personality characteristics` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the social score leads to detrimental or unfavourable treatment of certain natural persons or groups of persons in social contexts that are unrelated to the contexts in which the data was originally generated or collected` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the social score leads to detrimental or unfavourable treatment of certain natural persons or groups of persons that is unjustified or disproportionate to their social behaviour or its gravity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 5(1)(c) the AI practice is prohibited` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 5 the Chapter II provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 5 applies from 2 February 2025 (Article 113 third paragraph, point (a))
        IF NOT (    `the AI system is for the evaluation or classification of natural persons or groups of persons`
                AND `the evaluation or classification is over a certain period of time`
                AND `the evaluation or classification is based on their social behaviour or known, inferred or predicted personal or personality characteristics`
                AND (   `the social score leads to detrimental or unfavourable treatment of certain natural persons or groups of persons in social contexts that are unrelated to the contexts in which the data was originally generated or collected`
                     OR `the social score leads to detrimental or unfavourable treatment of certain natural persons or groups of persons that is unjustified or disproportionate to their social behaviour or its gravity`))
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): an element is missing; "either or both" of (i) and (ii) is enough, and neither is not covered
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Article 5(1)(d): predictive policing based solely on profiling`

-- src:185 | (d) the placing on the market, the putting into service for this specific purpose, or the use of an AI system for making risk assessments of natural persons in order to assess or predict the risk of a natural person committing a criminal offence, based solely on the profiling of a natural person or on assessing their personality traits and characteristics; this prohibition shall not apply to AI systems used to support the human assessment of the involvement of a person in a criminal activity, which is already based on objective and verifiable facts directly linked to a criminal activity;
@ref Art 5(1) first subparagraph point (d) (src:185)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the act` IS AN `Art 5(1) act`
      `the putting into service is for this specific purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is used for making risk assessments of natural persons in order to assess or predict the risk of a natural person committing a criminal offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the risk assessment is based solely on the profiling of a natural person or on assessing their personality traits and characteristics` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is used to support the human assessment of the involvement of a person in a criminal activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that human assessment is already based on objective and verifiable facts directly linked to a criminal activity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 5(1)(d) the AI practice is prohibited` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 5 the Chapter II provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 5 applies from 2 February 2025 (Article 113 third paragraph, point (a))
        IF NOT (    `Art 5(1) the act is within the practice` `the act` `the putting into service is for this specific purpose`
                AND `the AI system is used for making risk assessments of natural persons in order to assess or predict the risk of a natural person committing a criminal offence`
                AND `the risk assessment is based solely on the profiling of a natural person or on assessing their personality traits and characteristics`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): an element is missing (the specific purpose of a putting into service, the risk assessment, or its basis solely on profiling or personality traits)
        IF     `the AI system is used to support the human assessment of the involvement of a person in a criminal activity`
           AND `that human assessment is already based on objective and verifiable facts directly linked to a criminal activity`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "this prohibition shall not apply to AI systems used to support the human assessment of the involvement of a person in a criminal activity, which is already based on objective and verifiable facts directly linked to a criminal activity"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

