`Art 5(1)(g) the AI practice is prohibited` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 5 the Chapter II provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 5 applies from 2 February 2025 (Article 113 third paragraph, point (a))
        IF NOT (    `Art 5(1) the act is within the practice` `the act` `the putting into service is for this specific purpose`
                AND `the AI system is a biometric categorisation system that categorises individually natural persons based on their biometric data`
                AND `it categorises them to deduce or infer their race, political opinions, trade union membership, religious or philosophical beliefs, sex life or sexual orientation`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): an element is missing; the list of the characteristics (race ... sexual orientation) is closed by the point's own words, so another characteristic is not covered
        IF `the system does labelling or filtering of lawfully acquired biometric datasets, such as images, based on biometric data` OR `the system categorises biometric data in the area of law enforcement`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "this prohibition does not cover any labelling or filtering of lawfully acquired biometric datasets, such as images, based on biometric data or categorizing of biometric data in the area of law enforcement"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Article 5(1)(h): real-time remote biometric identification in publicly accessible spaces for law enforcement`

-- "the use ... unless and in so far as such use is strictly necessary for one of the following objectives": the exception is the text's own no.
-- "in so far as": the answer is about the use as a whole; where only part of a use is strictly necessary, the caller asks about each part (fork F-5-1-h-so-far-as).
-- Objective (iii) needs the offence to be referred to in Annex II and punishable in the Member State concerned by a custodial sentence or a detention order for a maximum
-- period of at least four years: "at least four years" is a threshold with four years inside it.
-- src:189 | (h) the use of ‘real-time’ remote biometric identification systems in publicly accessible spaces for the purposes of law enforcement, unless and in so far as such use is strictly necessary for one of the following objectives:
-- src:190 | (i) the targeted search for specific victims of abduction, trafficking in human beings or sexual exploitation of human beings, as well as the search for missing persons;
-- src:191 | (ii) the prevention of a specific, substantial and imminent threat to the life or physical safety of natural persons or a genuine and present or genuine and foreseeable threat of a terrorist attack;
-- src:192 | (iii) the localisation or identification of a person suspected of having committed a criminal offence, for the purpose of conducting a criminal investigation or prosecution or executing a criminal penalty for offences referred to in Annex II and punishable in the Member State concerned by a custodial sentence or a detention order for a maximum period of at least four years.
@ref Art 5(1) first subparagraph point (h) (src:189-192)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the act` IS AN `Art 5(1) act`
      `the AI system is a 'real-time' remote biometric identification system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the system is used in publicly accessible spaces` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is for the purposes of law enforcement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is strictly necessary for the targeted search for specific victims of abduction, trafficking in human beings or sexual exploitation of human beings, as well as the search for missing persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is strictly necessary for the prevention of a specific, substantial and imminent threat to the life or physical safety of natural persons or a genuine and present or genuine and foreseeable threat of a terrorist attack` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is strictly necessary for the localisation or identification of a person suspected of having committed a criminal offence, for the purpose of conducting a criminal investigation or prosecution or executing a criminal penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is referred to in Annex II` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the maximum period of the custodial sentence or detention order for the offence in the Member State concerned, in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 5(1)(h) the AI practice is prohibited` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 5 the Chapter II provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 5 applies from 2 February 2025 (Article 113 third paragraph, point (a))
        IF NOT (    `the act` EQUALS `Art 5(1) act use`
                AND `the AI system is a 'real-time' remote biometric identification system`
                AND `the system is used in publicly accessible spaces`
                AND `the use is for the purposes of law enforcement`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): point (h) prohibits "the use of 'real-time' remote biometric identification systems in publicly accessible spaces for the purposes of law enforcement"; the placing on the market and the putting into service are not in it
        IF     `the use is strictly necessary for the targeted search for specific victims of abduction, trafficking in human beings or sexual exploitation of human beings, as well as the search for missing persons`
            OR `the use is strictly necessary for the prevention of a specific, substantial and imminent threat to the life or physical safety of natural persons or a genuine and present or genuine and foreseeable threat of a terrorist attack`
            OR (    `the use is strictly necessary for the localisation or identification of a person suspected of having committed a criminal offence, for the purpose of conducting a criminal investigation or prosecution or executing a criminal penalty`
                AND `the offence is referred to in Annex II`
                AND `the maximum period of the custodial sentence or detention order for the offence in the Member State concerned, in years` AT LEAST 4)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless and in so far as such use is strictly necessary for one of the following objectives"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The last subparagraph: "Point (h) of the first subparagraph is without prejudice to Article 9 of Regulation (EU) 2016/679 for the processing of biometric data for purposes other than law enforcement."
-- JUST FALSE: point (h) does not affect Article 9 of that Regulation where the biometric data is processed for a purpose other than law enforcement.
-- NOTHING: the processing is for law enforcement, which the sentence does not speak to.
-- src:193 | Point (h) of the first subparagraph is without prejudice to Article 9 of Regulation (EU) 2016/679 for the processing of biometric data for purposes other than law enforcement.
@ref Art 5(1) last subparagraph (src:193)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the biometric data is processed for a purpose other than law enforcement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 5(1) last subparagraph point (h) affects Article 9 of Regulation (EU) 2016/679` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 5 the Chapter II provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 5 applies from 2 February 2025 (Article 113 third paragraph, point (a))
        IF `the biometric data is processed for a purpose other than law enforcement`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is without prejudice to Article 9 of Regulation (EU) 2016/679 for the processing of biometric data for purposes other than law enforcement"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the sentence says nothing of the processing of biometric data for law enforcement

§ `Article 5(1): any of the practices (seam S3 for Article 99)`

-- Article 99 (part P9) asks "the AI practice is prohibited under Article 5" as a yes-or-no input. This combiner takes the answers of the points the caller asked about:
-- JUST TRUE if any is JUST TRUE; NOTHING otherwise (a JUST FALSE is a carve-out of one point and does not make the practice prohibited under another). Fork F-S3: the list of points the caller asked about is not closed.
GIVEN `the answers of the points of Article 5(1)` IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 5(1) the AI practice is prohibited under one of the points` MEANS
    IF any (GIVEN r YIELD r EQUALS JUST TRUE) `the answers of the points of Article 5(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): no point the caller asked about prohibits the practice; the caller may not have asked about every point

-- The same as a yes-or-no for part P9 (seam S3): TRUE exactly when a point prohibits the practice.
GIVEN `the answers of the points of Article 5(1)` IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 5(1) seam S3 the AI practice is prohibited under Article 5` MEANS
    `Art 5(1) the AI practice is prohibited under one of the points` `the answers of the points of Article 5(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `Article 5(1): the prohibition as a rule`

DECLARE `Art 5(1) duty` IS ONE OF
    `Art 5(1) carry out the prohibited AI practice`

-- "The following AI practices shall be prohibited": the rule is that the practice is not carried out; the party is whoever places on the market, puts into service or uses,
-- and the text names none, so the party is `Operator` (the core has no constructor for "whoever carries out the practice"; compare Article 111(1)).
-- The duty arises only where a point prohibits the practice (JUST TRUE); otherwise nothing is owed.
-- src:175 | 1. The following AI practices shall be prohibited:
@ref Art 5(1) first subparagraph (src:175)
GIVEN `whether a point of Article 5(1) prohibits the AI practice` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 5(1) duty`
`Art 5(1) the duty not to carry out the prohibited AI practice` MEANS
    CONSIDER `whether a point of Article 5(1) prohibits the AI practice`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts
    WHEN JUST `prohibited` THEN
        IF `prohibited`
        THEN
            PARTY Operator
            SHANT `Art 5(1) carry out the prohibited AI practice`
            HENCE FULFILLED
            LEST BREACH BY Operator BECAUSE "the prohibited AI practice was carried out"
        ELSE FULFILLED  -- a carve-out applies: nothing is owed
